//! The ownership pass: every count a root's typed form holds, placed by one walk from each block's
//! end (Perceus over Lean's λRC). An owned value is let go of where it dies: after the instruction
//! that last reads it, before the one that last consumes something read out of it, or at the head
//! of a branch that does not read it. A use that consumes a value still live after it takes an
//! `Inc` first; a last use moves. A value read out of another keeps that one live until its own
//! last read, but where the other's last use consumes it before then: the value read out of it then
//! takes a count of its own where it is bound, so the other moves. A sum let go of where the case
//! around knows it to hold a boxed case, whose box a later boxed case of as many words is made in,
//! in the arms of the branch that follows or after it, with no stop, loop or handle between, is
//! opened into that box, which is reset into a token the make takes; a way out of the body between
//! frees it.
//! A flat value made or handed in whole, a loop's state at each pass among them, is opened into its
//! parts where it is bound, each part then counted on its own, so a leaf read out and consumed at
//! its last use moves; a field handed on out of a block this body holds is taken out of it, so
//! its count moves where the block is held only here. Each instruction that can fail names the
//! owned values held across it, which its failure path releases.
//!
//! Every `Inc` stands right before the instruction whose use it pays for, so an operand consumed
//! with no `Inc` of it just before is moved: a reader tells a move from a copy by the instruction
//! before it.

